  "body": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/svg+xml\" href=\"/favicon.svg\" />\n    <!-- People may zoom (WCAG 1.4.4; Submit and Save, 2026-10-12): no\n         maximum-scale, no user-scalable=no, and no script that cancels a\n         pinch. Form fields are at least 16px on a phone (index.css), which\n         is what keeps iOS from zooming in on focus. viewport-fit=cover was\n         tried and didn't address the iOS whitespace gap; it is back since\n         the navigation slice (2026-10-14) for the phone's bottom bar, which\n         sits above the home indicator through env(safe-area-inset-bottom)\n         (BottomBar.css). The page keeps clear of the side insets in\n         App.css (.app). -->\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\" />\n    <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#fafaf7\" />\n    <!-- Slice 11 follow-up: pre-CSS reset that loads before any\n         component stylesheet. Belt-and-braces against user-agent\n         default margins on iOS Safari and against any rogue padding\n         that creeps in via Vite's HMR ordering. The repeated\n         `!important` is intentional — these rules MUST win. -->\n    <style>html,body,#root{margin:0!important;padding:0!important}.app{min-height:100dvh}</style>\n    <!-- Slice 18 — title / OG metadata are env-driven via Vite's\n         Vite's %-placeholder substitution so per-deployment Vercel projects\n         (Floyd production, civic.social demo, future per-county\n         hubs) render their own branding from the same `main` build.\n         Defaults below match Floyd; overrides go in each Vercel\n         project's Production-scoped env vars. -->\n    <title>Civic Hub</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Vote on local issues, raise what matters, and see where your community stands.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Civic Hub\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Vote on local issues, raise what matters, and see where your community stands.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <!-- Static OG image. The SPA can't inject per-vote OG tags\n         (crawlers don't run JS), so every shared link unfurls\n         with the Hub banner + generic title. Per-vote OG would\n         need a server-side bot-detection rewrite (Slice 15.1\n         candidate). -->\n    <meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:image:alt\" content=\"\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n    <script type=\"module\" crossorigin src=\"/assets/main-BU7bKBix.js\"></script>\n    <link rel=\"modulepreload\" crossorigin href=\"/assets/errorReporter-Ca1HBXUt.js\">\n    <link rel=\"modulepreload\" crossorigin href=\"/assets/settingOwners-BapYKNXT.js\">\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" crossorigin href=\"/assets/settingOwners-CnsLAKhl.css\">\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" crossorigin href=\"/assets/main-BWuQlMDJ.css\">\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
